### Important Context
- 1.2 did raw RSA-OAEP(SHA512) over whole files: fails above ~382 bytes (RSA-4096).
- v2 layout: `sha512("pyencrypto:v2") | mode`, then
  - mode 0x01 RSA: `u16 len | RSA-OAEP(32-byte AES key) | 12-byte nonce | AES-GCM(data)`
  - mode 0x02 symmetric: `12-byte nonce | AES-GCM(data)`
  - header (everything before ciphertext) is GCM associated data.
- v1 files (`sha512("pyencrypto") | raw RSA-OAEP`) still decrypt via `decrypt_data`.
- `encrypt_bytes`/`decrypt_bytes` unchanged (raw RSA). New byte API: `encrypt_data`/`decrypt_data`.
- Symmetric key files: urlsafe-base64 of 32 random bytes, created 0600 with O_EXCL.
- Max data size 2**31-1 bytes (AESGCM limit); whole file is held in memory.
- Homebrew python3 uses a non-editable wheel install (installer: uv). Rebuild + reinstall after source changes:
  `uv build && uv pip install --system --break-system-packages --reinstall --no-deps dist/pyencrypto-1.3-py3-none-any.whl`
- sdist excludes `.ai` via `[tool.hatch.build.targets.sdist]`.

